## Auth

OAuth 2.1, via the `oauth.ts` module next to `index.ts` — PKCE, a local
loopback redirect listener, on-disk token caching (`0600` permissions),
and refresh-before-expiry, all proven unchanged across three real
providers (Slack, Google Drive, Notion) in the original catalog.

**Before you assume your provider matches the defaults**, check:
- Does it require PKCE? (`usesPkce`)
- Does it issue refresh tokens, and under what conditions?
- Does its token endpoint want form-urlencoded credentials in the body,
  or Basic auth + JSON? (`tokenAuthStyle` — Notion needed the latter;
  don't assume form-urlencoded "just works" until you've checked)
- Does it do real scope negotiation, or a different access model
  entirely (Notion: capability + explicit per-page sharing)?

Fill in `authorizeUrl`, `tokenUrl`, `scopes`, and `tokenAuthStyle` (if
needed) in `index.ts` from your provider's actual OAuth documentation —
never assume.
